# Run db:migrate and start local BE first. No ebook is guaranteed to remain available.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@workId = OL15328717W
@editionId = OL23747519M

### Inspect selected edition and its parent work before adding
GET https://openlibrary.org/books/{{editionId}}.json

### Inspect reading availability; exact match required by our backend
GET https://openlibrary.org/api/volumes/brief/olid/{{editionId}}.json

### Read-only detail: readingUrl is a trusted link or null
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/{{workId}}

### Add selected edition; persists readingUrl in books (201 or 409 if already added)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workId": "{{workId}}",
  "editionId": "{{editionId}}"
}

### Verify persisted metadata: data.book.readingUrl
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}

### Reload detail; ebook section is hidden if readingUrl is null
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/{{workId}}

### Client-provided URLs are rejected (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workId": "{{workId}}",
  "readingUrl": "https://example.com/"
}
